  "type": "MCQ",
  "question": "The line \\(2x+3y-k=0\\) with \\(k>0\\) cuts the \\(x\\)-axis and \\(y\\)-axis at points \\(A\\) and \\(B\\) respectively. Then the equation of the circle having \\(AB\\) as diameter is",
  "options": {
    "A": "\\(x^2+y^2-\\frac{k}{2}x-\\frac{k}{3}y=k^2\\)",
    "B": "\\(x^2+y^2-\\frac{k}{3}x-\\frac{k}{2}y=k^2\\)",
    "C": "\\(x^2+y^2-\\frac{k}{2}x-\\frac{k}{3}y=0\\)",
    "D": "\\(x^2+y^2-\\frac{k}{3}x-\\frac{k}{2}y=0\\)"
  },
  "answer": "C",
